-- 0039  Reference vocabulary: the picklists a fresh install starts with.
-- =============================================================================
-- This is data, not schema, and it was dumped from the running migration
-- machine on 2026-09-16: the waste types the state form asks about, the
-- service-type catalog the ledger's lines reference by code, the system-type
-- and baffle vocabularies the pickers (DRV-08) sit on, the counties and their
-- legacy aliases, and a starter bid price list. None of it is company
-- history: no people, no properties, no disposal sites. A company deploying
-- clean gets the same vocabulary the ledger was built against instead of
-- empty dropdowns.
--
-- Every statement is conflict-guarded, because on the migrated database
-- these rows arrived through the ETL with different ids — the inserts address
-- natural keys (name, code, alias), never ids.
SET search_path TO septic_app, pg_catalog;

